  "title_sa": "संख्याशब्दाः - संख्येयशब्दाः",
  "title_en": "Sabdamanjari — Numerals Reference Chart (Cardinals and Ordinals, 3 through 1,00,00,000)",
  "source": "Sabdamanjari (शब्दमञ्जरी), Samskrit Education Society",
  "source_pdf_pages": "108-114 (printed page numbers; physical PDF pages 109-115)",
  "relation_to_main_corpus": "Companion file to sabdamanjari_vibhakti_tables_from_page_5_2.json (the main corpus file). The main corpus file covers pratipadika words 1-185, the last of which (185, द्वितीय नपुंसकलिङ्ग) is the final word in the book given a full 8-case declension table. This file transcribes the nominative-only numerals reference chart that follows immediately after word 185 in the book, which the main corpus file's extraction_summary explicitly notes was deferred to a separate file.",
  "schema_note": "Unlike the main corpus file's words[].declension_table (8 case-rows x vachana/gender columns), the source here prints ONLY nominative-singular forms, by gender, for each number's cardinal and ordinal. Accordingly each entry below has flat 'cardinal'/'ordinal' objects with pum/stri/napum keys (or a single shared citation field where the book gives one form for all/most genders), not a declension_table. Where the book prints two alternate spellings for one cell, they are hyphen-joined in that one field, matching the main corpus file's convention. Where the book prints entirely separate alternate words/paradigms, they are recorded as a list under 'alternates' / 'ordinal_alternates' / 'ordinal_alt_tama', each note-annotated.",
  "general_declension_rules": [
    "9 (नव) and 10 (दश) are not separately tabled in the book; a note after word 177 (सप्तन्) states they decline like सप्तन्.",
    "Ordinals from 'तृतीय' (3rd) onward, other than the fully-tabled words 183-185 (द्वितीय), are not separately tabled; the book's explicit rule (PDF p.108, following word 185) states: 'चतुर्थ-पञ्चमादयः शब्दाः सर्वेऽपि — पुंसि राम शब्दवत्; स्त्रियां नदी शब्दवत्; क्लीबे फल शब्दवत् द्रष्टव्याः' — i.e. all ordinals from the 4th onward decline: masculine like राम (word 1), feminine like नदी (ईकारान्त, e.g. पद्धतिः — the नदी paradigm itself is not a separate word in this corpus), neuter like फल (word 3).",
    "एकोनविंशति (19), विंशति (20), षष्टि (60), सप्तति (70), अशीति (80), नवति (90) and कोटि (1,00,00,000) — the इकारान्त feminine cardinal nouns — decline like मति (इकारान्त स्त्रीलिङ्ग); मति itself is not a separate word in this corpus.",
    "त्रिंशत् (30), चत्वारिंशत् (40), पञ्चाशत् (50) — the दकारान्त cardinal nouns — decline like सरित् (दकारान्त स्त्रीलिङ्ग); सरित् itself is not a separate word in this corpus.",
    "शतं (100), सहस्रं (1000), अयुतं (10,000), लक्षं (1,00,000), प्रयुतं (10,00,000) — the नपुंसकलिङ्ग round numbers — decline like वनम् (word 4, अकारान्त नपुंसकलिङ्ग).",
    "PDF p.114 closes with a note that alternate '-तम' ordinal-compound forms (विंशतितम, त्रिंशत्तम, ... प्रायशः) are commonly used for the round tens (20, 30, ... 90) and for 99, in addition to the shorter forms shown in the main columns; both are recorded here where printed."
  ],
